<!DOCTYPE softwarelist SYSTEM "softwarelist.dtd">
<!--
license:CC0-1.0

    Roland SRX wave expansion boards, 32 MB each and word-wide, for the
    XV-3080, the XV-5080 and their relatives.  The board carries its own
    label in the clear at offset 0 of the scrambled image, "Roland SRX  "
    and then the magic 4F B0 58 A7 and the sixteen-byte identity the host
    compares, and the socket undoes eighteen permuted address lines within
    each 256 KB block and the eight data lines.

    Each entry is commented with that identity, with the name the machine
    shows and with the build date the board stamps ten bytes after it, all
    read from the descrambled image.  The year is that build date.

    Every image here is marked BAD_DUMP because no board has been read.
    Each is Roland's own wave data as their plugins carry it, where it is
    already descrambled, put back into board form by the inverse of the
    socket's permutation; the data is expected to be the board's, but
    nothing here testifies to that.  The two PG-SRX images carry their own
    later build dates, and the list takes each entry's year from the date
    its image stamps.

    Not here: the rest of the SRX boards.
-->

